  "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{\\pi (1+{t}^{6})}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({t}^{3})}{\\pi }|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{3})}{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
